        "answer": "Not as a blanket rule for every current CHAMPVA claim. 38 CFR § 17.276 generally requires the OHI claim to be filed and the other payer to issue a final payment determination or EOB before CHAMPVA pays. The regulation that expressly requires an OHI appeal first is 38 CFR § 17.277, and that section applies only to legacy claims, with limited exceptions such as when the OHI says the issue is non-appealable.",
