    "summary": "Practical VA Community Care resources covering referrals and authorizations, how Community Care differs from private insurance, and what Veterans should know about provider billing rules.",
    "body_markdown": "## About this category\n\nVA Community Care can be confusing because eligibility, referrals, authorizations, scheduling, continued-care requests, provider billing, and private insurance are separate issues.\n\nUse the articles in this category to understand:\n\n- how Community Care referrals and authorizations work;\n- how continued care and Request for Service (RFS) requests are handled;\n- how VA health care and Community Care differ from ordinary private insurance;\n- what to do when a Community Care provider bills a Veteran directly;\n- the rules around balance billing and missed-appointment fees; and\n- which official VA or Community Care Network source to use when a provider needs billing guidance.\n\nThese resources are educational. Authorization details, network administration, and local workflows can change, so confirm the current status of an individual referral or bill with VA or the applicable Community Care Network administrator.\n\n*Last researched: September 17, 2026.*",
